---
// Table 6 of Feng et al. (2019), "Temporal Relational Ranking for Stock Prediction":
// cumulative investment return ratio (IRR), mean with the +- the paper prints, for the model with no
// graph (Rank_LSTM) and three ways of adding the industry-relation graph. Numbers copied from the paper.
const W = 900;
const H = 330;
const rows = [
  { en: 'No graph', vi: 'Không graph', m: [0.68, 0.60], n: [0.56, 0.68] },
  { en: 'GCN', vi: 'GCN', m: [0.24, 0.32], n: [0.97, 0.56] },
  { en: 'RSR_E', vi: 'RSR_E', m: [0.20, 0.22], n: [1.00, 0.58] },
  { en: 'RSR_I', vi: 'RSR_I', m: [0.23, 0.27], n: [1.06, 0.27] },
];
const SC = 230 / 1.8; // px per 1.0 of IRR, axis -0.2 .. 1.6
const panels = [
  { x0: 36, key: 'm', en: 'NASDAQ: 1,026 stocks', vi: 'NASDAQ: 1.026 mã' },
  { x0: 468, key: 'n', en: 'NYSE: 1,737 stocks', vi: 'NYSE: 1.737 mã' },
];
const LBL = 92;
---
<figure class="atp18-rsr">
  <div class="atp18-scroll">
    <svg viewBox={`0 0 ${W} ${H}`} role="img" aria-label="Cumulative return ratio of a stock-ranking model with and without an industry-relation graph. On NASDAQ the no-graph model scores 0.68 with a spread of 0.60 while the three graph models score 0.24, 0.20 and 0.23. On NYSE the no-graph model scores 0.56 with a spread of 0.68 while the graph models score 0.97, 1.00 and 1.06. Every graph bar overlaps the no-graph bar.">
      <text x="36" y="24" class="h">
        <tspan data-lang-en>The same graph helped on one market and hurt on the other</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>Cùng một graph: giúp ở sàn này, hại ở sàn kia</tspan>
      </text>
      {panels.map((p) => (
        <g>
          <rect x={p.x0} y="44" width="396" height="238" rx="8" class="panel" />
          <text x={p.x0 + 14} y="68" class="t">
            <tspan data-lang-en>{p.en}</tspan>
            <tspan data-lang-vi>{p.vi}</tspan>
          </text>
          {[0, 0.5, 1, 1.5].map((v) => (
            <g>
              <line x1={p.x0 + LBL + (v + 0.2) * SC} x2={p.x0 + LBL + (v + 0.2) * SC} y1="82" y2="248" class="grid" />
              <text x={p.x0 + LBL + (v + 0.2) * SC} y="266" text-anchor="middle" class="tick">{v.toFixed(1)}</text>
            </g>
          ))}
          {rows.map((r, k) => {
            const [mean, sd] = r[p.key as 'm' | 'n'];
            const base = rows[0][p.key as 'm' | 'n'][0];
            const y = 100 + k * 40;
            const x = p.x0 + LBL + (mean + 0.2) * SC;
            const lo = p.x0 + LBL + (mean - sd + 0.2) * SC;
            const hi = p.x0 + LBL + (mean + sd + 0.2) * SC;
            const cls = k === 0 ? 'base' : mean < base ? 'worse' : 'better';
            return (
              <g>
                <text x={p.x0 + 14} y={y + 4} class="lab">
                  <tspan data-lang-en>{r.en}</tspan>
                  <tspan data-lang-vi>{r.vi}</tspan>
                </text>
                <line x1={lo} x2={hi} y1={y} y2={y} class={`bar ${cls}`} />
                <line x1={lo} x2={lo} y1={y - 5} y2={y + 5} class={`bar ${cls}`} />
                <line x1={hi} x2={hi} y1={y - 5} y2={y + 5} class={`bar ${cls}`} />
                <circle cx={x} cy={y} r="5.5" class={`dot ${cls}`} />
              </g>
            );
          })}
        </g>
      ))}
      <text x="36" y="308" class="note">
        <tspan data-lang-en>Dot: mean return ratio over the 237 test days. Bar: mean ± the spread the paper prints. Red: worse than no graph. Gold: better.</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>Chấm: return ratio trung bình trên 237 ngày test. Thanh: trung bình ± độ lệch bài báo in ra. Đỏ: tệ hơn không có graph. Vàng: tốt hơn.</tspan>
      </text>
    </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption>
    <span data-lang-en>Table 6 of Feng et al. (2019), industry relations. On both markets the bar of every graph model overlaps the bar of the model with no graph, so these runs alone cannot separate them.</span>
    <span data-lang-vi>Bảng 6 của Feng và cộng sự (2019), quan hệ ngành. Ở cả hai sàn, thanh của mọi mô hình có graph đều chồng lên thanh của mô hình không graph, nên chỉ riêng các lần chạy này chưa tách được chúng.</span>
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .atp18-rsr { margin: 2em 0; width: 100%; }
  .atp18-scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
  .atp18-rsr svg { display: block; width: 100%; min-width: 640px; height: auto; }
  .atp18-rsr .h { font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; fill: var(--text); }
  .atp18-rsr .t { font-size: 13.5px; font-weight: 700; fill: var(--text); }
  .atp18-rsr .lab { font-size: 13px; fill: var(--text-body); }
  .atp18-rsr .tick { font-size: 11.5px; fill: var(--text-muted); }
  .atp18-rsr .note { font-size: 12.5px; fill: var(--text-muted); }
  .atp18-rsr .panel { fill: var(--bg-alt); stroke: var(--border); }
  .atp18-rsr .grid { stroke: var(--border); stroke-width: 1; }
  .atp18-rsr .bar { stroke-width: 2; fill: none; }
  .atp18-rsr .bar.base { stroke: var(--text-muted); }
  .atp18-rsr .bar.worse { stroke: var(--red); }
  .atp18-rsr .bar.better { stroke: var(--gold); }
  .atp18-rsr .dot.base { fill: var(--text-muted); }
  .atp18-rsr .dot.worse { fill: var(--red); }
  .atp18-rsr .dot.better { fill: var(--gold); }
  .atp18-rsr figcaption { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.55; text-align: center; }
</style>
